    "lawCode": "Amd §1229-c, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3623A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in\nrelation to requiring children under the age of 8 to be restrained by\na child restraint system in a motor vehicle\n\n PURPOSE OF THE BILL :  This bill would enhance highway safety for\nchildren who are passengers in motor vehicles.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :  Section 1 of the bill would amend Vehicle\nand Traffic Law (\"VTL\") § 1229-c(1)(b) to increase, to age 7, the\nmaximum age at which children over the age of four are required to be\nrestrained in booster seats while they are passengers in the back seat\nof an automobile.\n\nSection 2 of the bill would make the same amendment to VTL, §\n1229-c(2)(e), regarding front seat passengers.\n\nSections 3 and 4 of the bill would make conforming amendments to VTL\n§§ 1229-c(6) and (12), respectively, concerning the increased maximum\nage of child passengers subject to the booster seat requirement.\n\nSection 5 of the bill would provide that the bill would take effect 90\ndays after it becomes law.\n\n EXISTING LAW : Currently, the VTL requires only children ages four\nthrough six to be restrained in child passenger restraint systems.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :  A.11083-A passed the Assembly in 2007.\nrestrained in child passenger restraint systems.\n\n STATEMENT IN SUPPORT :  Pursuant to two recent enactments (Chapter\n509 of the Laws of 2004 and Chapter 18 of the Laws of 2005), ages four\nthrough six are required to be restrained in special booster seats, as\nare those under four who weigh more than forty pounds. However,\naccording to the Center for Disease Control growth charts, while 95%\nof children under the age of eight weigh less than 80 pounds. All\ncurrent booster seats are certified for at least 80 pounds and many,\nup to 100 pounds. The average eight year old is about 50\" tall (4 feet\n2inches) and 96% of this age group are under 54\" (4 feet 6 inches).\nDue to the difference in anatomy between adults and children, the\nrecommended height to use an adult seat belt is 4 feet 9 inches.\nTherefore, including 7 year olds in the booster seat requirement is a\nreasonable step that recognizes the reality of the physical size of\nthis age group, and will enhance the safety of these children when\nthey are passengers in an automobile.\n\n BUDGET IMPLICATIONS :  None.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :  This bill would take effect 90 days after receiving\nExecutive approval.\n",
